        {
          "id": "909a4c49-9119-3d60-9208-e4de5a7121d6",
          "content": {
            "id": "909a4c49-9119-3d60-9208-e4de5a7121d6",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Champion Homes (SKY) Is Up 12.3% After Proposed Chassis Rule Repeal Signals Regulatory Tailwind Potential",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Recently, analyst Meredith Whitney highlighted proposed US House and Senate bills that would repeal an outdated chassis requirement for manufactured homes, a reform that could materially lower production costs and support wider adoption of factory-built housing across the country. This push to modernize federal rules could reshape the economics of manufactured housing, potentially strengthening the competitive position of producers such as Champion Homes within the broader housing supply...",
